# Public Repo Safety

This repository is public. Never include secrets or Intuit-internal information in code, docs, commit messages, PR text, or examples.

- Do not commit credentials or secrets (API keys, tokens, passwords, private certs, cookies, `.env` values, connection strings).
- Do not include Intuit-internal identifiers or content (internal URLs, hostnames, Slack channels, Jira links/IDs, customer/internal IDs, runbooks, wiki text, incident details).
- Replace sensitive values with safe placeholders like `YOUR_API_KEY`, `example.com`, and `PROJECT-123`.
- Before proposing a commit, explicitly check staged changes for sensitive strings and remove/redact anything risky.
- If a user asks to commit sensitive data, refuse and suggest secure alternatives (env vars, secrets manager, local-only files, `.env.example`).

## Pre-commit Safety Checklist

- Verify no secrets are present in changed files.
- Verify no Intuit-specific internal information is present.
- Ensure examples and logs are sanitized.
